<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ data.title }}</title>
<link rel="icon" href="data:,">
<style>
  :root { --accent: #1f5f8b; --rule: #d0d0d0; --muted: #666666; }
  body { font-family: -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #222; margin: 0 auto;
         max-width: 1200px; padding: 16px 24px 40px 24px; line-height: 1.45; font-size: 14px; }
  h1 { font-size: 22px; margin: 0 0 4px 0; }
  h2 { font-size: 17px; color: var(--accent); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-bottom: 3px;
       margin-top: 36px; }
  h3 { font-size: 14px; margin: 18px 0 6px 0; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  nav { font-size: 13px; margin: 10px 0 0 0; }
  nav a { margin-right: 14px; color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12px; margin: 8px 0; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 2px 6px; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap; }
  th { background: #f4f4f4; font-weight: 600; }
  td.n { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  table.alleles td { text-align: center; min-width: 34px; }
  table.alleles thead th { text-align: center; }
  table.wide thead th { white-space: normal; vertical-align: bottom; max-width: 90px; word-break: break-word; }
  thead th { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 2; }
  tbody th { position: sticky; left: 0; z-index: 1; }
  tbody tr:hover td, tbody tr:hover th { filter: brightness(0.96); }
  table.kv th, table.kv td { white-space: normal; }
  table.kv { max-width: 100%; }
  table.kv th { width: 160px; }
  .scroll { overflow: auto; max-width: 100%; max-height: 78vh; }
  details summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent); margin: 6px 0; }
  code, pre { font-family: "SFMono-Regular", Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 12px; }
  pre { background: #f7f7f7; border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 8px; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre-wrap;
        word-break: break-all; }
  figure { margin: 14px 0 22px 0; }
  figure svg { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
  figcaption, .caption { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 4px; }
  .caption b, figcaption b { color: #222; }
  p.tcap { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); margin: 14px 0 2px 0; }
  p.tcap b { color: #222; }
  .lead { background: #f4f8fb; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding: 6px 10px; margin: 10px 0; }
  .methods { max-width: 900px; text-align: justify; }
  ul.failures li { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .legend { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); }
  .swatch { display: inline-block; width: 12px; height: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); margin: 0 4px 0 12px;
            vertical-align: middle; }
  footer { margin-top: 40px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 8px; font-size: 12px;
           color: var(--muted); }
  @page { size: A4 landscape; margin: 12mm; }
  @media print { body { max-width: none; font-size: 11px; padding: 0; }
                 details { display: block; } details > *:not(summary) { display: block; } nav { display: none; }
                 h2 { page-break-after: avoid; } figure, tr { page-break-inside: avoid; }
                 .scroll { max-height: none; overflow: visible; }
                 table { font-size: 9px; } thead th, tbody th { position: static; } th, td { padding: 1px 4px; }
                 a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>{{ data.title }}</h1>
<p class="meta">Generated {{ generated }} by mlvatyper {{ version }} with merPCR {{ merpcr_version }}.</p>
<table class="kv">
{% for key, value in meta %}
<tr><th>{{ key }}</th><td>{{ value }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
<nav>
  <a href="#summary">Summary</a><a href="#alleles">Allele profiles</a><a href="#figures">Figures</a>
  <a href="#evidence">Evidence</a><a href="#missing">Missing markers</a>
  {% if discovery_table %}<a href="#discovery">Discovery</a>{% endif %}
  <a href="#methods">Methods</a><a href="#appendix">Appendix</a>
</nav>

{% set n = namespace(t=0, f=0) %}
{% macro tcap(text) %}{% set n.t = n.t + 1 %}<p class="tcap"><b>Table {{ n.t }}.</b> {{ text }}</p>{% endmacro %}
{% macro fcap(text) %}{% set n.f = n.f + 1 %}<b>Figure {{ n.f }}.</b> {{ text }}{% endmacro %}

<h2 id="summary">1. Summary</h2>
<p class="lead">{{ meta_completeness }}</p>
{% if screening %}
<h3 id="across">Across samples</h3>
<p>Share of loci with status OK per sample: mean {{ screening.mean }}, lowest {{ screening.min }}.
{% if screening.low %}Samples below 75%: {{ screening.low | join(", ") }}.{% else %}No sample is below 75%.{% endif %}
The per-sample and per-locus tables are written as <code>{{ prefix }}_sample_summary.tsv</code> and
<code>{{ prefix }}_locus_summary.tsv</code>.</p>
{% if screening.concerns_table %}
<p><b>Loci to review.</b> A flag on more than half of the typed calls of a locus, or an allele of zero or
below, points at the scheme (reference values, repeat unit or patterns) more often than at the strains.</p>
{{ tcap("Loci to review.") }}
<div class="scroll">{{ screening.concerns_table | safe }}</div>
{% else %}
<p>No locus carries one flag on more than half of its calls, and no allele is zero or below.</p>
{% endif %}
<details><summary>Per locus: typed, OK, missing, most frequent flag and diversity</summary>
{{ tcap("Calls per locus. Share is the part of the typed calls that carry the most frequent flag; the Simpson index is computed over the integer alleles.") }}
<div class="scroll">{{ screening.loci_table | safe }}</div></details>
{% if screening.missing_table %}
<details><summary>Missing products by reason</summary>
{{ tcap("Combinations of sample and marker without a product, by the reason established by the search.") }}
<div class="scroll">{{ screening.missing_table | safe }}</div></details>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
<h3>Per sample</h3>
<p>Markers typed are those with an integer repeat number; missing markers have no amplicon. The remaining
columns count status codes per sample; a marker can carry several codes.</p>
<details{% if n_samples <= 20 %} open{% endif %}><summary>Typing completeness and status codes for {{ n_samples }} samples</summary>
{{ tcap("Typing completeness and status codes per sample.") }}
<div class="scroll">{{ summary_table | safe }}</div></details>
{% if failures %}
<ul class="failures">
{% for code, explanation, items in failures %}
  <li><strong>{{ code }}</strong> ({{ items | length }}): {{ explanation }}.
      <span class="meta">{{ items[:12] | join(", ") }}{% if items | length > 12 %}, ...{% endif %}</span></li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% else %}
<p>Every marker was found in every sample without flags.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="alleles">2. Allele profiles</h2>
<p>Repeat numbers per marker in STS order{% if transposed %}, markers as rows because they outnumber the
samples{% endif %}. Several amplicons for one marker are joined with a slash. Cells are shaded by status code.</p>
{{ legend | safe }}
{{ tcap("Allele profiles. Abbreviations in place of a number are explained above and in the appendix; hover over a cell for the full code.") }}
<div class="scroll">{{ alleles_table | safe }}</div>
<details><summary>Profile strings (hyphen joined, the MLVAbank input format)</summary>
<div class="scroll">{{ profile_table | safe }}</div></details>

<h2 id="figures">3. Figures</h2>
{% if data.figures.heatmap %}
<h3>Relationships between samples</h3>
<figure>{{ data.figures.heatmap | safe }}
<figcaption>{{ fcap("Clustered allele profiles. Rows are samples ordered by UPGMA clustering (Sokal and Michener 1958) on the categorical coefficient, the share of loci that differ among the loci typed in both samples, which is the usual way of comparing MLVA profiles; columns are loci in STS order. Each locus has its own colour scale, from the lowest to the highest repeat number seen in it, and the repeat number is printed in the cell when the matrix is small. Grey cells have no single integer allele. The tree shows distance on a scale of 0 to 1.") }}</figcaption></figure>
{% if data.figures.distance %}
<figure>{{ data.figures.distance | safe }}
<figcaption>{{ fcap("Pairwise distances in the order of the heatmap: the share of loci that differ, among loci typed in both samples. Pairs that share fewer than 8 typed loci are given the mean distance. Alleles are compared as categories, so the distance does not reflect the size of the repeat difference.") }}</figcaption></figure>
{% endif %}
{% if data.figures.mst %}
<figure>{{ data.figures.mst | safe }}
<figcaption>{{ fcap("Minimum spanning tree of the distinct allele profiles, built on the same categorical distance with the tie-breaking rules of goeBURST (Francisco et al. 2009): among equal edges the node with more single, double and triple locus variants, then the node that stands for more samples, is linked first. Samples with identical profiles share a node (size shows how many, the label gives the first sample and the number of others). Edge labels give the number of loci that differ between neighbours. Node colour is the share of OK calls, so a poorly typed sample can be told from a distant one. The layout places nodes so that straight-line distances approximate distances along the tree; it is a drawing, and only the tree and the edge labels carry information.") }}</figcaption></figure>
{% endif %}
{% if data.figures.mds %}
<figure>{{ data.figures.mds | safe }}
<figcaption>{{ fcap("Classical multidimensional scaling of the pairwise distances in two dimensions. The axis labels give the share of the distance structure that each axis keeps; a low total means that two dimensions describe the samples poorly and the heatmap and the tree should be read instead.") }}</figcaption></figure>
{% endif %}
{% if data.figures.spectra %}
<figure>{{ data.figures.spectra | safe }}
<figcaption>{{ fcap("Allele spectrum per locus: the number of samples with each repeat number.") }}</figcaption></figure>
{% endif %}
{% if data.figures.callrate %}
<figure>{{ data.figures.callrate | safe }}
<figcaption>{{ fcap("Share of calls with status OK per locus (top) and per sample (bottom), sorted. Loci or samples at the left or top of the sorted bars are those to inspect first.") }}</figcaption></figure>
{% endif %}
<h3>Amplicons and status</h3>
{% endif %}
<figure>{{ data.figures.lengths | safe }}
<figcaption>{{ fcap("Amplicon length per marker (points, one per amplicon) and the expected size from the STS file (grey tick).") }}</figcaption></figure>
<figure>{{ data.figures.residuals | safe }}
<figcaption>{{ fcap("Residual between the amplicon length and the expected size of the called allele. Values other than zero indicate flanking indels, primer indels or a wrong unit length.") }}</figcaption></figure>
<figure>{{ data.figures.status | safe }}
<figcaption>{{ fcap("Status per sample and marker; the first flag of a call sets the colour, and white cells are OK.") }}</figcaption>
</figure>

<h2 id="evidence">4. Evidence per amplicon</h2>
<p>One row per amplicon: coordinates on the contig, length, expected size and residual in bp, primer mismatches
and indels, the search pass that found it (main, rescue, aligned), the allele and the tandem array count with
its exact and variant windows. Rows with a flag are shaded.</p>
{% for sample in data.samples %}
<details{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}><summary>{{ sample }}</summary>
{% if loop.first %}{{ tcap("Evidence per amplicon, one table per sample.") }}{% endif %}
<div class="scroll">{{ evidence[sample] | safe }}</div></details>
{% endfor %}

<h2 id="missing">5. Markers without amplicon</h2>
{% if missing_table %}
{{ tcap("Markers without an amplicon and the reason established by the search.") }}
<div class="scroll">{{ missing_table | safe }}</div>
{% else %}
<p>None.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if discovery_table %}
<h2 id="discovery">6. Repeat unit discovery</h2>
<p>{{ discovery_summary }} Categories: A strong (unit of 5 bp or more, 3 or more copies, score and entropy
above threshold), B plausible (2 copies), C weak (short unit, low score or overlap with a primer). Mixed
markers hold two or more non-overlapping A or B candidates.</p>
<details><summary>Discovery report, primary candidate per marker</summary>
<div class="scroll">{{ discovery_table | safe }}</div></details>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="methods">{{ "7" if discovery_table else "6" }}. Methods</h2>
<p class="methods">{{ methods }}</p>
<h3>Software</h3>
{{ tcap("Software used and the references to cite.") }}
<table><thead><tr><th>software</th><th>reference</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for name, url, reference in software %}
<tr><td>{{ name }} ({{ url }})</td><td>{{ reference }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
<h3>Command line</h3>
<pre>{{ command }}</pre>
{% if inputs %}
<h3>Input files</h3>
{{ tcap("Input files with size and MD5 checksum.") }}
<table><thead><tr><th>file</th><th>size (bytes)</th><th>MD5</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for item in inputs %}
<tr><td>{{ item.path }}</td><td>{{ item.size }}</td><td><code>{{ item.md5 }}</code></td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
{% endif %}
<details><summary>Recorded parameters (run_info.json)</summary><pre>{{ parameters }}</pre></details>

<h2 id="appendix">{{ "8" if discovery_table else "7" }}. Appendix</h2>
{% if definitions_table %}
<h3>Marker definitions used</h3>
<details><summary>Definitions</summary>{{ tcap("Marker definitions used for this prefix.") }}<div class="scroll">{{ definitions_table | safe }}</div></details>
{% endif %}
<h3>Status codes</h3>
{{ tcap("Status codes and their meaning.") }}
<table><thead><tr><th>code</th><th>meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for code, meaning in glossary.items() %}
<tr><td>{{ code }}</td><td>{{ meaning }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>

<footer>Report written by mlvatyper {{ version }} from the tables in {{ data.outdir }}; regenerate with
<code>mlvatyper report --outdir {{ data.outdir }} --prefix {{ prefix }}</code>.</footer>
</body>
</html>
